load 0
=== bcftools
--- bcftools 
annotate 	annotate and edit VCF/BCF files
call 	SNP/indel calling
cnv 	HMM CNV calling
concat 	concatenate VCF/BCF files from the same set of samples
consensus 	create a consensus sequence by applying VCF variants
convert 	convert VCF/BCF files to different formats and back
csq 	call variation consequences
filter 	filter VCF/BCF files using fixed thresholds
gtcheck 	check sample concordance, detect sample swaps and contamination
head 	view VCF/BCF file headers
help 	show help for a command
index 	index VCF/BCF files
isec 	intersections of VCF/BCF files
merge 	merge VCF/BCF files from non-overlapping sample sets
mpileup 	multi-way pileup producing genotype likelihoods
norm 	left-align and normalize indels
plugin 	user-defined plugins
polysomy 	detect the number of chromosomal copies
query 	transform VCF/BCF into user-defined formats
reheader 	modify the VCF/BCF header, change sample names
roh 	identify runs of autozygosity (HMM)
sort 	sort a VCF/BCF file
stats 	produce VCF/BCF stats
view 	convert, view, subset and filter VCF/BCF files
--- bcftools vie
view 	convert, view, subset and filter VCF/BCF files
--- bcftools view -
--force-samples 	only warn about unknown subset samples
--no-version 	do not append the version and command line to the header
--regions-overlap=	include if POS is in the region (0), the record overlaps (1), the variant overlaps (2)
--targets-overlap=	include if POS is in the region (0), the record overlaps (1), the variant overlaps (2)
--threads=	use multithreading with INT worker threads
--verbosity=	verbosity level
--with-header 	print both the header and the records (the default)
-A 	remove '<*>' or '<NON_REF>' at variant sites (-AA: at all sites)
-C 	maximum count of the non-reference alleles
-G 	drop the genotype information (after subsetting)
-H 	suppress the header in VCF output
-I 	do not recalculate the INFO fields for the subset
-M 	maximum number of alleles listed in REF and ALT
-O 	u/b: un/compressed BCF, v/z: un/compressed VCF (then 0-9: compression level)
-P 	exclude sites where all samples are phased
-Q 	maximum frequency of the non-reference alleles
-R 	restrict to the regions listed in a file
-S 	file of samples to include
-T 	like -R but streams rather than jumps by the index
-U 	exclude sites without a called genotype
-V 	exclude variant types
-W 	automatically index the output files
-X 	exclude sites where the non-reference alleles are private to the subset
-a 	trim the ALT alleles not seen in the genotypes
-c 	minimum count of the non-reference alleles
-e 	exclude sites for which the expression is true
-f 	require at least one of the listed FILTER strings
-g 	require hom, het or missing genotypes (or exclude with ^)
-h 	print only the header in VCF output
-i 	select sites for which the expression is true
-k 	known sites only (ID is not '.')
-l 	compression level, from 0 to 9
-m 	minimum number of alleles listed in REF and ALT
-n 	novel sites only (ID is '.')
-o 	write the output to FILE
-p 	sites where all samples are phased
-q 	minimum frequency of the non-reference alleles
-r 	restrict to a comma-separated list of regions
-s 	comma-separated list of samples to include
-t 	like -r but streams rather than jumps by the index
-u 	sites without a called genotype
-v 	select variant types: snps,indels,mnps,ref,bnd,other,overlap
-x 	sites where the non-reference alleles are private to the subset samples
--- bcftools view --
--apply-filters=	require at least one of the listed FILTER strings
--compression-level=	compression level, from 0 to 9
--drop-genotypes 	drop the genotype information (after subsetting)
--exclude-phased 	exclude sites where all samples are phased
--exclude-private 	exclude sites where the non-reference alleles are private to the subset
--exclude-types=	exclude variant types
--exclude-uncalled 	exclude sites without a called genotype
--exclude=	exclude sites for which the expression is true
--force-samples 	only warn about unknown subset samples
--genotype=	require hom, het or missing genotypes (or exclude with ^)
--header-only 	print only the header in VCF output
--include=	select sites for which the expression is true
--known 	known sites only (ID is not '.')
--max-ac=	maximum count of the non-reference alleles
--max-af=	maximum frequency of the non-reference alleles
--max-alleles=	maximum number of alleles listed in REF and ALT
--min-ac=	minimum count of the non-reference alleles
--min-af=	minimum frequency of the non-reference alleles
--min-alleles=	minimum number of alleles listed in REF and ALT
--no-header 	suppress the header in VCF output
--no-update 	do not recalculate the INFO fields for the subset
--no-version 	do not append the version and command line to the header
--novel 	novel sites only (ID is '.')
--output-type=	u/b: un/compressed BCF, v/z: un/compressed VCF (then 0-9: compression level)
--output=	write the output to FILE
--phased 	sites where all samples are phased
--private 	sites where the non-reference alleles are private to the subset samples
--regions-file=	restrict to the regions listed in a file
--regions-overlap=	include if POS is in the region (0), the record overlaps (1), the variant overlaps (2)
--regions=	restrict to a comma-separated list of regions
--samples-file=	file of samples to include
--samples=	comma-separated list of samples to include
--targets-file=	like -R but streams rather than jumps by the index
--targets-overlap=	include if POS is in the region (0), the record overlaps (1), the variant overlaps (2)
--targets=	like -r but streams rather than jumps by the index
--threads=	use multithreading with INT worker threads
--trim-alt-alleles 	trim the ALT alleles not seen in the genotypes
--trim-unseen-allele 	remove '<*>' or '<NON_REF>' at variant sites (-AA: at all sites)
--types=	select variant types: snps,indels,mnps,ref,bnd,other,overlap
--uncalled 	sites without a called genotype
--verbosity=	verbosity level
--with-header 	print both the header and the records (the default)
--write-index	automatically index the output files
--- bcftools view -O 
b 	compressed BCF
u 	uncompressed BCF
v 	uncompressed VCF
z 	compressed VCF
--- bcftools view --output-type=
--output-type=b 	compressed BCF
--output-type=u 	uncompressed BCF
--output-type=v 	uncompressed VCF
--output-type=z 	compressed VCF
--- bcftools view --regions-overlap 
0 	POS is in the region
1 	the record overlaps the region
2 	the variant overlaps the region
--- bcftools view -v 
bnd 
indels 
mnps 
other 
overlap 
ref 
snps 
--- bcftools view data/
data/calls.bcf 
data/calls.vcf.gz 
--- bcftools view data/calls.vcf.gz 
chr1 
chr2 
--- bcftools view -r 
--- bcftools view data/calls.bcf -r c
chr1 
chr2 
--- bcftools view -s 
--- bcftools view data/calls.vcf.gz -s s
