sampleB 
--- bcftools view -R data/
data/regions.bed 
--- bcftools view -o out.vcf data/
data/calls.bcf 
data/calls.vcf.gz 
--- bcftools view -W
-W 	automatically index the output files
--- bcftools view --write-index=
--write-index=csi 
--write-index=tbi 
=== other subcommands
--- bcftools index -
--threads=	use multithreading with INT worker threads
-a 	with --stats, print the stats of all contigs, even when zero
-c 	generate a CSI index (the default)
-f 	overwrite the index if it exists
-m 	minimal interval size for CSI indices, 2^INT
-n 	print the number of records, from the existing index
-o 	the name of the index file
-s 	print the per-contig stats, from the existing index
-t 	generate a TBI index (VCF only)
-v 	verbosity level
--- bcftools index data/
data/calls.bcf 
data/calls.vcf.gz 
--- bcftools annotate -a data/
data/a.bam 
data/calls.bcf 
data/calls.vcf.gz 
data/regions.bed 
--- bcftools annotate --pair-logic 
all 
both 
exact 
id 
indels 
snps 
some 
--- bcftools concat -d 
all 
both 
exact 
indels 
snps 
--- bcftools concat -
--ligate-force 	ligate even non-overlapping chunks, keep all sites
--ligate-warn 	drop sites in imperfect overlaps
--naive-force 	like --naive, without the header check (dangerous)
--no-version 	do not append the version and command line to the header
--regions-overlap=	include if POS is in the region (0), the record overlaps (1), the variant overlaps (2)
--threads=	use multithreading with INT worker threads
-D 	alias for -d exact
-G 	drop the genotype information
-O 	u/b: un/compressed BCF, v/z: un/compressed VCF (then 0-9: compression level)
-R 	restrict to the regions listed in a file
-W 	automatically index the output files
-a 	the first coordinate of the next file may precede the last record of this one
-c 	output the PS tag only at the start of a phase set block
-d 	output duplicate records present in several files once
-f 	read the list of files from a file
-l 	ligate phased VCFs by matching the phase at overlapping haplotypes
-n 	concatenate without recompression, with a header compatibility check
-o 	write the output to FILE
-q 	break the phase set if the phasing quality is lower than INT
-r 	restrict to a comma-separated list of regions
-v 	verbosity level
